From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:43:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 103/118] Node DFA life information with exception edges for
 the register variables of procedures with try

Procedures with exception handling (pi_uses_exceptions) got no node DFA, so
their loops kept every register variable used in them live across the back
edge (get_used_live_regvars needs life information) and the register variable
rule of optexcregvar had to be conservative.

SetNodeSucessors now handles try..except, on and try..finally nodes and
records in optinfo^.excsucc where an exception raised in a protected block
continues (the first on handler, the default handler, the finally block, or
after the statement for an empty except block); the life computation adds
the life of that node to every node of the block. For procedures with
exception handling (no labels, no assembler), this life information is
created after the node transformations, which stay off (excdfaavailable, not
pi_dfaavailable). It is used by the loop register sync, and by
optexcregvar: a by-value scalar or a single-field record written in a
protected block is unsafe only when it is live where the exception continues;
other variables, self and the result keep the old rule.
vm2: Frame, self and Template in registers, the per-instruction scratch values
no longer live across the loop (cycles -14%, instructions -4.3%);
tests/test/texcregvar3.pp.
